<title>NETHERLANDS: KLM to merge British marketing with Air UK.</title>
<headline>KLM to merge British marketing with Air UK.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch carrier KLM said on Tuesday it would merge its British sales and marketing division with that of 45 percent-owned Air UK from April 1.</p>
<p>&quot;The merger is aimed at creating a stronger organisation in the U.K market...and will generate economies of scale,&quot; KLM spokesman Hans Leijte said.</p>
<p>He said the two carriers currently generated annual turnover of some 400 million sterling in the British market, but added that the synergies created by the merger were expected to &quot;substantially increase&quot; this figure over the coming years.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
